  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Other Africa Grants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project protects the wildlife of Conkouati Douli National Park in the Republic of Congo by reducing illegal wildlife trafficking in and around the park. It conserves chimpanzees, gorillas, forest elephants, and marine turtles by tackling poaching and bushmeat trade through a comprehensive and targeted law enforcement strategy. Specific activities include building the capacity of the ecoguard force and establishing a wildlife crime unit composed of community liaisons, lawyers and data analysts.</narrative>
  </description>
